WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:06.636
Joan calls these simple marks: about twenty abbreviations, worth maybe five marks.

2
00:00:06.636 --> 00:00:10.014
She'll give you a prescription and ask what it means.

3
00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:11.607
Say each one before I do.

4
00:00:12.057 --> 00:00:12.535
<v Examiner>O D?

5
00:00:12.535 --> 00:00:13.013
<v Examiner>B D?

6
00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.730
<v Examiner>T D S?

7
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.447
<v Examiner>Q I D?

8
00:00:14.897 --> 00:00:15.621
Once a day.

9
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:16.411
Twice a day.

10
00:00:16.411 --> 00:00:17.596
Three times a day.

11
00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:18.715
Four times a day.

12
00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:20.069
<v Examiner>Q four H?

13
00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:20.872
<v Examiner>Q six H?

14
00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:22.565
Every four hours.

15
00:00:22.565 --> 00:00:23.734
Every six hours.

16
00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:29.071
And Q six H is not the same as Q I D: four times a day fits waking hours,

17
00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:31.775
every six hours runs round the clock.

18
00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:32.854
<v Examiner>P R N?

19
00:00:32.854 --> 00:00:33.377
<v Examiner>Stat?

20
00:00:33.827 --> 00:00:34.665
As required.

21
00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:36.131
Immediately, at once.

22
00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:36.998
<v Examiner>Mane?

23
00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:37.499
<v Examiner>Nocte?

24
00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:38.895
In the morning.

25
00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:39.463
At night.

26
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:40.824
<v Examiner>And A C?

27
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:41.279
<v Examiner>P C?

28
00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:43.464
Before meals, ante cibum.

29
00:00:43.464 --> 00:00:46.379
After meals, post cibum: post means after.

30
00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:47.356
<v Examiner>P O?

31
00:00:47.356 --> 00:00:47.882
<v Examiner>S L?

32
00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:48.408
<v Examiner>P R?

33
00:00:48.858 --> 00:00:49.464
By mouth.

34
00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:52.226
Sublingual, under the tongue, like G T N.

35
00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:52.698
Rectal.

36
00:00:53.148 --> 00:00:54.428
<v Examiner>I M, I V, S C?

37
00:00:54.878 --> 00:00:57.566
Intramuscular, intravenous, subcutaneous.

38
00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:58.827
<v Examiner>Topical?

39
00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:04.013
Applied directly to a body surface: skin creams, eye drops, ear drops.

40
00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:04.912
<v Examiner>E C?

41
00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:06.148
<v Examiner>S R or C R?

42
00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:09.621
Enteric-coated: it resists the stomach's acid.

43
00:01:09.621 --> 00:01:11.986
Slow release, or controlled release.

44
00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:13.169
Never crush these.

45
00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.904
<v Examiner>Diclofenac sixty micrograms Q I D P R?

46
00:01:17.354 --> 00:01:20.242
Sixty micrograms, four times a day, rectally.

47
00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:23.066
Her point: it's not about diclofenac at all.

48
00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.055
You just read the prescription.

49
00:01:25.505 --> 00:01:26.394
And two rules.

50
00:01:26.394 --> 00:01:30.966
Times are in the twenty-four-hour clock, so eighteen hundred is six p m.

51
00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:33.569
Only the prescriber can change the route.

52
00:01:34.019 --> 00:01:40.438
Abbreviations: O D once, B D twice, T D S three times, Q I D four times a day.

53
00:01:40.438 --> 00:01:42.577
Q four H every four hours.

54
00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:44.058
P R N as required.

55
00:01:44.058 --> 00:01:45.128
Stat at once.

56
00:01:45.128 --> 00:01:49.653
Mane morning, nocte night, A C before meals, P C after.

57
00:01:49.653 --> 00:01:53.521
P O by mouth, S L under the tongue, P R rectal.

58
00:01:53.521 --> 00:01:58.293
E C enteric-coated; S R and C R slow release, never crush.

59
00:01:58.293 --> 00:02:01.420
Only the prescriber changes the route.
